hadiths[150]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8024","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad al-Daqqaq told us in Baghdad, Abd al-Karim bin al-Haytham told us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhib reported, saying: I heard Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, speaking, on the authority of Amra bint Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Two inscriptions were found on the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The most arrogant of people is a man.” He strikes someone other than the one who struck him, and a man kills someone other than his killer, and a man befriends someone other than those who were blessed by him. Whoever does that has disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and it will not be accepted. “There is no morphology or justice from it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “And it is witnessed by the hadith of Abu Shurayh Al-Adawi, who
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8024 - True"
"8025","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid Al-Laythi, on the authority of Abu Shuraih Al-Adawi, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Among the people most cruel to God Almighty is he who kills someone other than his killer, or seeks the blood of the people of Islam in pre-Islamic times, and who He looked with his eyes in sleep as long as they did not see. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it except Yunus bin Yazid, who narrated it on the authority of Al-Zuhri with a chain of narration. Another"
"8026","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told us, about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muslim bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Shuraih Al-Kaabi, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with this hadith
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8025 - True"
"8027","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Kurayb told us, and Nasr bin Ali told us, they said: We told us Abu Ahmad Al-Zubayri, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the morning comes, Satan sends out his forces and says: Whoever misleads a Muslim today, I will wear a crown on him, and he will come.” One of them says: I did not stay with him until he divorced his father. He said: He is about to divorce him, and one of them comes and says: I did not stay with him until he divorced him. His wife, so he says: He is about to get married, and one of them comes and says: I have not stayed with him until he commits polytheism, so he says: You, and one of them comes. He says: I did not stay with him until he was killed. Then he says: You, and he wears the crown. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8027 - True"
"8028","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Sulayman bin Harb told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, that Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, attended the day of the house and said: I adjure you by God Almighty, you know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in one of three cases: adultery after chastity, or Apostasy after Islam, or killing a person unjustly, for which he is to be killed. “By God, I have not committed adultery during ignorance or Islam, nor have I apostatized since.” “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I did not kill the soul that God has made sacred, so why are you killing me?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8028 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8029","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim al-Razi told us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ali bin told us Abdul Hamid Al-Kinani, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad Al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him On their authority, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A person will remain within the limits of his religion as long as he has not shed unlawful blood.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, but rather it is counted among the individuals of Muhammad bin Yahya al-Dhuhli, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya al-Kinani, and he has Another authentic chain of narration.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8029 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8030","Abu Al-Abbas Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told us, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, Ishaq bin Saeed bin Amr told us. Ibn Sa`id Ibn Al-Aas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A person will not cease to be in He is free from his religion as long as he does not shed any unlawful blood.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8030 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8031","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa told us, Thawr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Abi Aoun, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, said: I heard Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan, and he spoke very little on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All sins may be forgiven by God, except for a man who dies as an unbeliever, or a man who intentionally kills a believer.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8031 - True"
"8032","Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Al-Balkhi, the merchant in Baghdad, told me, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ahmed told us, Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak told us. Al-Dimashqi, Sadaqa told us, Khalid bin Dahqan told us, Abdullah bin Abi Zakaria told us, he said: I heard Umm al-Darda’ saying: I heard Abu Darda’ May God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “All sins may be forgiven by God, except for a man who dies as a polytheist or “He kills a believer intentionally.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8032 - True"
"8033","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Salama bin Qais Al-Ashja’i, he said: It is only four, and I am not as old today as the day I was. I heard them from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Do not associate anything with God. “And do not kill the soul that God has forbidden except for what is right, and do not steal, and do not commit adultery.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8033 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8034","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Al-Hussein bin Abi Ma’shar told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Aidh, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever meets God Almighty, not associating anything with Him, and does not mourn the blood of an unlawful person, will enter Paradise through any of the gates of Paradise he wishes.” It has been said On the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8034 - True"
"8035","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Al-Hasan bin Sufyan told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Numayr told us, Al-Qasim bin Al-Walid told us Al-Hamdani, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever dies not associating anything with God, and has not mourned the blood of a forbidden person, may enter through any gate of Paradise he wishes.” It was narrated about this. “The chapter on the authority of Atiya al-Awfi is a hadith that I have not seen narrated, and I have also commented on it.”"
"8036","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq the Imam told us, Ubaid bin Hatim the Hafiz, known as the calf, informed us. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us. Ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baghawi, Dawud ibn Abd al-Hamid told us - he was originally from Kufa and moved to Mosul - Amr bin Qays told us. Al-Mala’i, on the authority of Attiya Al-Awfi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: A person was killed during the reign of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the city, he went up to the pulpit as a preacher and said: “Do you know who killed this dead man before you?” Three times, they said: By God, we do not know of him as a killer. Then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if they gathered together to kill a believer, the inhabitants of heaven And the people of the earth were satisfied with him, God would admit them all to Hell, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no one hates us, Ahl al-Bayt, except that God will cast him into Hell. ""fire""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8036 - Fake news"
"8037","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Asbat bin Nasr Al-Hamdani told us, Ismail bin Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No “The believer will be destroyed. Faith is subject to destruction.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8037 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8038","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Attab Al-Abdi informed us in Baghdad, Ahmad bin Ubaid Allah Al-Narsi told us, Amr bin Asim told us Al-Kalabi, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Marwan bin Al-Hakam, he said: I entered with Muawiyah, to visit Umm The Believers Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: O Muawiyah, you killed Hujr and his companions and did what you did. Are you not afraid that he will hide for you? A man and he kills you? He said: No, I am in a safe house. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Faith is subject to lethality. No believer can be lethal.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8038 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8039","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Ghalib, said: Ammar entered Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the Day of the Camel, and said: Peace be upon you, mother. She said: You have no mother. He said: Yes, you are my mother, even if you hate it. She said: Who is the one whose voice I hear with you? He said: Al-Ashtar. She said: O Ashtar, are you the one who wanted to kill my sister’s son? He said: I was keen to kill him, and he was keen to kill me, but he could not. She said: By God, if I had killed him, I would not have succeeded. As for you, Ammar? You have learned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one shall be killed except three: a man who kills another man and is killed by him, and a man who commits adultery after A chaste man, and a man who apostatized from Islam. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8039 - True"
"8040","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Mahdi bin Rustum Al-Asbahani told us, Abu Amer Al-Aqdi, Qurra bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, he said: Amer bin Shaddad told us, he said: I was concealing something by lying. I entered upon him with my sword, and one day I entered upon him and he said: You have come to me, by God, and Gabriel has risen from this throne, so I fell to the point of my sword. So I said: I could not wait to walk between his head and his body until I mentioned a hadith that Amr ibn al-Hamq, may God be pleased with him, told us: I heard the Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “If a man was reassured by another man and then killed him after he was reassured by him, a banner will be set up for him on the Day of Resurrection. “Treachery” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8040 - True"
"8041","Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Khalifa told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not permissible The blood of a man from the people of the qiblah, except in one of three cases: he is killed and will be killed, the married adulterer, and the one who separates from the community. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8041 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8042","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, Muhammad bin Issam told us, Hafs bin Abdullah told us, and Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Daoud Al-Alawi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Hafiz told us, Ahmad bin Hafs told us, my father told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ya’mar, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her She said: “It is not permissible to shed the blood of anyone from the people of the qiblah except in one of three cases: a man who is killed and he should be killed for him, a married man who commits adultery, and a man who separates ""For the group"""
"8043","Ahmad bin Kamil al-Qadi told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa al-Qadi told us, Abu Hudhayfah told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman told us, on the authority of Mansour, On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the same."
"8044","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Isa bin Al-Sakan told us, through Wasit, Abu Mansour Al-Harith bin Mansour told us, we told us Israel, Othman Al-Shaham narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: She was the mother of a son of a man who had Among them were two sons like two pearls, and she used to curse the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, but he forbade her and would not stop, and he would rebuke her and she would not rebuke, so when It was one night when she mentioned the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he could not wait until he got up and went to Mughal and placed her in her womb and then leaned on her until He carried it out, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I bear witness that her blood was shed.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration on the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8044 - True"
"8045","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Attardi told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Abu Barza, he said: Abu Bakr became angry with a man, so I said: Who is he, O successor of the Messenger of God? May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Why?” I said: I will behead him if you order me to do so. He said: Then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: “Did you do it?” I said: Yes, he said: By God, I will remove the severity of the word that I said that made him angry. Then he said: “It has not happened to anyone after Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Sahih. The chain of transmission is based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8045 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8046","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Nasrabadi informed us, Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hana’i informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh told us, Ubayy told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Repentance of Al-Anbari, he said: I heard Abu Al-Sawwar Abdullah bin Qudamah bin Anza Al-Qadi, speaking on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: The most cruel man is Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him. So I said: O successor of the Messenger of God, should I not kill him? He said: “This is only for those who insulted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8046 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8047","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Amr, Mawla al-Muttalib, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever you find working The people of Lot did the deed, so kill the subject and the object.”
 Suleiman bin Bilal said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed and Rabi’ah saying: “Whoever does the actions of the people of Lot must be stoned, whether he is married or not.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it and have a witness.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8047 - True"
"8048","Ahmad bin Sahl, the jurist in Bukhara, told us. Abu Ismah Sahl bin Al-Mutawakkil told us, Al-Qa’nabi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Omar Al-Omari, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who “He did the actions of the people of Lot, so stone the subject and the object.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8048 - Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Omar Al-Amri has fallen"
"8049","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abdullah bin Jafar Al-Mukhrami, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever you find doing the actions of the people of Lot, kill the subject and the object, and whoever you find committing an animal, kill him and the animal.” “With him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. And for the addition in mentioning the animal, there is a witness.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8049 - True"
"8050","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Abbad bin Mansour told me, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned that he said about the one who seizes the animal: “Kill the one who does it.” And the object of it”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8050 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8051","Abu Al-Walid told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Issa told us, Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, said: “Whoever has sex with an animal is not subject to any punishment.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8051 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8052","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told me, Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God curse whoever slaughters for anyone other than God. May God curse the one who changes the borders of the earth, may God curse the one who turns the blind from the path, may God curse the one who curses his parents, may God curse the one who turns away from his friends, May God curse whoever did the actions of the people of Lot.” He said: Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Amr bin Abi Amr told us, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who added to it: “May God curse whoever falls upon an animal.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8052 - True"
"8053","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah Ahmad bin Al-Faraj told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, Harun Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God has cursed seven of His creation.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, responded. May God bless him and grant him peace three times, then he said: “Cursed is cursed. Cursed is he who does what the people of Lot did. Cursed is he who has intercourse with a woman.” And her daughter, cursed is he who curses any of his parents, cursed is he who commits any of the animals, cursed is he who changes the borders of the land, cursed is he who slaughters For anyone other than God. Cursed be he who follows other than his followers.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8053 - Harun bin Harun Al-Taymi is weak"
"8054","Ali bin Hamshadh, Al-Adl told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Ibn Abi Maryam told us, Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habiba told us, Dawud bin Al-Husayn told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever falls on A mahram woman, then kill him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8054 - Incorrect"
"8055","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Asbat bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, Mutarrif bin Tarif Al-Harithi narrated to us, Abu Al-Jahm narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Aazib, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Indeed, I go around looking after camels of mine that have gone astray.” So I was wandering around in verses, and suddenly I was with a rider and horsemen. Then the people of the water made them seek refuge in my house, and they circumambulated my courtyard and extracted from it a man. They had not spoken to him until they had beheaded him. When they had gone, I asked about him, and they said: He was married to his father’s wife.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8055 - True"
"8056","Zayd ibn Abi Unaisa told us, on the authority of Adi ibn Thabit, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Bara’, on the authority of his father, who said: I met my uncle, and he had the flag, so I said to him: Where do you want? He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to a man who had had intercourse with his father’s wife, so he ordered me to behead him and take his money.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8056 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8057","Hammam told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Wahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed What I fear most for my nation is the action of the people of Lot.” Authentic chain of narration.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8057 - True"
"8058","Wahib told us, on the authority of Abu Waqid, on the authority of Ishaq, the client of Zaida, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever guards what is between his two beards and his feet will enter Paradise.” The chain of transmission is authentic, and Abu Waqid is Saleh bin Muhammad.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8058 - True"
"8059","Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever God protects from the evil of what is between his beard and his feet He entered Paradise.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8059 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8060","Israel told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, the client of al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, on the authority of al-Mughirah, he said: It was mentioned by Sa’d ibn Ubadah. A man came to his father’s wife and said: If I caught him, I would strike him with a sword. I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “I am jealous.” By God, I am more jealous of Saad than me, and there is no one to whom an excuse is more beloved than God. That is why He sent the messengers, and there is no one to whom I love praise. From God, and for that is the promise of Paradise.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. Abu Awanah named this servant of al-Mughirah in his narration. And he brought the body on his face.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8060 - True"
"8061","Just as Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Warad, the scribe of al-Mughirah, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, he said: Sa’d ibn Ubadah said: If I saw a man with His father’s wife struck him with an unarmored sword. This was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Are you amazed at Saad’s jealousy? By God, because I am more jealous than him, and God is more jealous than me, and because of God’s jealousy, He forbade immoral acts, whether apparent or hidden, and no one “I am more jealous than God, and there is no person to whom I would prefer an excuse. For that, he was promised Paradise.”"
"8062","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Shaddad bin Sa’id told us, Sa’id bin Iyas Abu Masoud Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O “Youth of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. For him who keeps his private parts will have Paradise.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8062 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8063","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, from the origin of his book, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid told us, Al-Ma’afah bin Suleiman Al-Harrani told us, we told him Musa bin Ayan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Aqeel, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Abu Darda’ and I were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard him say: “Whoever guards what is between his mouth and his feet will enter Paradise.”"
"8064","Abu Bakr told me, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, Musa bin Ayan told us, with this chain of transmission similar to it. However, he said: On the authority of Aqeel
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8063 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8065","Abu Bakr told me, Muhammad bin Ayyub told me, Abu Al-Rabi’ told us, Omar bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad May God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever puts his trust in Me between his two jaws and what is between his feet, I will trust for him Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8065 - This in Al-Bukhari"
"8066","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Al-Musayyab bin Zuhair Al-Baghdadi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Ismail bin Jafar told us, Amr bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ensure I have six things from among you that I guarantee for you Paradise: Be truthful when you tell the truth, fulfill your promise when you are entrusted with it, and guard your private parts. And lower your eyes, and restrain your hands. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.” This is witnessed by the hadith of Saad bin Sinan, on the authority of Anas, who
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8066 - There is a transmission"
"8067","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Saad bin Sinan, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Accept me six May I accept Paradise for you? They said: What is it? He said: “When one of you speaks, let him not lie, and when he makes a promise, let him not break it, and if he is entrusted with it, let him not betray it. And lower your eyes, and withhold your hands. And guard your private parts.”"
"8068","Ahmad bin Kamil al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad al-Awfi told us, Ruh bin Ubadah told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: Ahmad bin Sa’d told us Muhammad bin Isa Al-Qadi, Abu Al-Nu’man told us Muhammad bin Al-Fadl, Hammad bin Zaid told us, all on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, he said: Ubayy bin said to me Ka'b, and he was reciting Surat Al-Ahzab. He said: I said: seventy-three verses. He said: “Cat.” I said: Never. He said: “I have seen it, and it is equal to al-Baqarah, and we have read in what we have read about it: The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them. Of course, it is a punishment from God, and God is Mighty, Wise. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8068 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8069","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us, Muhammad bin Musa Al-Bashani told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein informed us Ibn Waqid, Yazid the grammarian told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Whoever disbelieves in stoning has disbelieved in the Qur’an.” In a way that does not count His saying, the Almighty, the Almighty: O People of the Book, Our Messenger has come to you, making clear to you much of what you were concealing from the Book. So the stoning was something they concealed: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8069 - True"
"8070","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Al-Layth told me Bin Saad, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Marwan bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, that his aunt told him She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, read to us the verse about stoning: “When an old man or a woman commits adultery, stone them absolutely for what they have decided.” “From pleasure.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8070 - True"
"8071","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ja`far, Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Kathir ibn al-Salt, he said: It was Ibn al-Aas, and Zayd ibn Thabit They were writing the Qur’an, so they passed over this verse, and Zaid said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When the old man and the old woman commit adultery So stone them absolutely.” Amr said: “When it was revealed, I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Should I write it down? It was as if he hated that.” Then Amr said to him: “Don’t you see that if the old man commits adultery while married, he is flogged and stoned, and if he is not married, he is flogged, and “If a married man commits adultery while he is married, he will be stoned.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8071 - True"
"8072","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Abdullah bin Hamran told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Yunus ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Kathir ibn al-Salt, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “When an old man or a woman commits adultery, stone them absolutely.”"
"8073","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah, and Al-Hasan bin Abdul-Samad told us, they said: Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah reported, Ismail bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jundub Al-Khair, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Hadd “The magician is struck by a sword.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and if the two sheikhs left out the hadith of Ismail bin Muslim, then it is strange and authentic. “A true witness to the condition of them all against this.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8073 - Sahih Gharib"
"8074","Professor Abu Al-Walid told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Thumama Ibn Uqba Al-Muhallimi, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Arqam, said: “A man was entering upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man bewitched him, so he made a necklace for him and he put it on.” And he threw him into the well of an Ansar man, and two angels came to him to visit him. One of them sat at his head and the other sat at his feet, and he said One of them: Do you know what caused his pain? He said: So-and-so who had consummated his marriage contracted for him and threw him into the well of so-and-so the Ansari. If only he had sent for him. A man took the necklace from him and found that the water had turned yellow. He did not mention any of it to him, nor did he blame him. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it."
"8075","We were told by Abu Abd al-Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi al-Wazir, the merchant. Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris al-Hanzali told us, By Al-Ray, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Ash'ath bin Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that one of the princes of Kufa invited a sorcerer. He was playing in front of the people. He reached a grasshopper, so he approached his sword and embraced it. When he saw it, he struck it with his sword, and the people dispersed from him. He said: “O you!” People, you will not be heeded. Rather, I wanted the magician, so the prince took him and imprisoned him. This was reported to Salman, and he said: “What a miserable thing they have done. This should not have happened.” He is a trusted imam who invites a magician to play with him, and this person should not blame his prince with the sword.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8075 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8076","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, my father told us, he said: I heard Ya`la bin Hakim narrated, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Ma’iz bin Malik: “Woe to you, perhaps you kissed, touched, winked, or looked.” He said: No. He said: “Did you do it?” He said: Yes, then he ordered that he be stoned. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.” Al-Hakam bin Aban narrated it, on the authority of Ikrimah, with extra words
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8076 - This in Al-Bukhari"
"8077","As Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Maruzi told us, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl told us, Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni told us, Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a goat came to a Muslim man and said: I committed an indecent act. So what do you command me? So the man said to him: Go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ask forgiveness for you. Then a goat came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked his words - or he said: his words - and then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to those who were with him: “Has your companion been touched?” Ibn Abbas said: I looked at the people to advise them, but none of them turned to me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Perhaps you kissed it.” He said: No. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “So you touched it.” He said: No. He said: “So you did something to it and it was not?” He said: Yes. He said: “Then stone him.” He said: While he was being stoned, the man to whom a goat had come to consult him threw a bone at him, and a goat fell down and turned around. To him, a goat said to him: God killed you when you saw me, and now you are stoning me.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8077 - Hafs bin Imran Al-Adni, they declared it weak"
"8078","Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih and Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Anazi told us, saying: Muadh ibn Najda al-Qurashi told us, Khallad ibn Yahya told us, Bashir bin Al-Muhajir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came Al-Aslami Ma’iz bin Malik, and he said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery and I want you to purify me. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Go back.” So he returned until he came the third time, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to his people and asked them, and they praised him well. He said: “How is his mind?” Is he mad? They said: No, by God, and they praised him well for his mind and religion. He came to him the fourth time and asked them about him, and they told him the same thing, so he ordered them. So they dug a hole for him up to his chest, then stoned him. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim. He used Bashir ibn Muhajir as evidence.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8078 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8079","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuli told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Dawud bin Abu Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that Ma’iz bin Malik came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: I committed an indecent act. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, repeatedly rejected him and asked his people: “Is there something wrong with him?” They said: There is nothing wrong with him except that he did something that he did not think could bring him out of it unless the punishment was meted out to him. He said: So he gave us the command and we set off with it. To Baqi al-Gharqad. He said: We did not dig for it, nor did we bind it. We threw potsherds, bones, and sandalwood at it, but it remained still. So he ran, and we rallied behind him. Then he came to Al-Hurra and set himself up for us, and we threw him with her puppies until he calmed down. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose in the evening to give a sermon, thanked God and praised Him. He said: “As for what follows, what is the matter with people when we invade, and one of them is left behind among our families, having a brother like the husband of a goat? As for me, I will not take anyone.” “Who among them did that, except that I punished him” He said: He did not curse him nor did he ask forgiveness for him. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8079 - according to the conditions of Al-Nasa’i and Muslim"
"8080","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hazzal, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Hazzal, if you covered him With your garment, it will be better for you.” Shu’bah said: Yahya said: So I mentioned this hadith in a gathering in which Yazid bin Nu’aym bin Hazal was present, and he said Yazid: “This truth is truth and it is a serious hadith.” “This is a hadith with a sound chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.” Abu Dawud was unique in this addition. About Shu'bah
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8080 - True"
"8081","Abu Muhammad Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Suleiman Al-Hadrami told us, Ali bin Saeed bin Stolen Al-Kindi, Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with On his authority, he said: It was said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: When a goat found that it touched stones and death, it fled, so he said: “Will you not leave it?” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8081 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8082","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmed bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Yazid bin Nu’aym, on the authority of his father, said: Ma’iz bin Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery, so stand against me. The Book of God, so he turned away from it until he came four times. He said: “Take him and stone him.” When the stones touched him, he became frightened and became more severe. He said: So he came out. Abdullah bin Unais, from his desert, shot him with a donkey’s back and struck him, and people threw at him until they killed him, so his escape was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he said: “Will you leave him alone, perhaps he will repent and God will forgive him?” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8082 - True"
"8083","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Bashir bin Muhajir told us, Abdullah bin Buraydah, on the authority of his father, said: A woman from Ghamid came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: I have committed suicide, and he said: “Go,” so she went, then She came back and said: Perhaps you want to do to me what you did to Ma’iz bin Malik. By God, I am pregnant. So he said: “Go until you give birth.” Then she came. With him in a rag, she said: I have given birth, so purify me. He said: “Go until you wean him.” So she went and brought him a piece of bread in his hand, so she said: She weaned him, so he ordered her to be stoned. It was narrated by Ibrahim bin Maymun Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8083 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8084","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sunni informed us of Marw, Abu Al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abu Hamza informed, then Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have committed adultery, so stand up. He said: “Go and put what is in your stomach.” When she had put what was in her stomach, she came to him and said: I have committed adultery, so carry out the punishment. So he said: “Go until you wean your child.” When she weaned her child, she came and said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery, so fulfill the punishment. He said: “Bring me someone who will pay for it.” Your child.” Then a man stood up and said: “I will sponsor her child.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned her. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim.” They did not take it out, and Malik ibn Anas narrated in Al-Muwatta’ the hadith of the stoning with a chain of transmission for which I fear it may be sent.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8084 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8085","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Malik told me Ibn Anas, on the authority of Yaqoub Ibn Yazid Ibn Talha al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, that a woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said that she She committed adultery while she was pregnant, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Go until you give birth.” So she went, and when she gave birth, she came to him, and he said: “Go until you give birth.” You breastfeed him.” When she breastfed him, she came to him, and he said: “Go until you entrust him to him.” When she entrusted him, she came to him, and he imposed the punishment on her. “This is a hadith. It is valid according to the conditions of the two sheikhs if Yazid bin Talha al-Taymi caught up with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Malik bin Anas, the ruling on the hadith of the Madinians.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8085 - According to the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim, if Yazid Al-Taimi caught up with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"8086","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman bin Al-Hassan Al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, Abu Al-Ahwas Muhammad bin Al-Haytham Al-Qadi told us, Abd told us Al-Ghafar bin Daoud Al-Harrani, Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “I have never seen a man more violent than Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him. A woman from Hamadan, called Sharahah, was brought and flogged.” One hundred, then he ordered her to be stoned, so Ali took a brick and threw it at her, but the root of her ear did not miss any of it, so he struck her, and the people stoned her until They killed her, then he said: I flogged her according to the Book of God Almighty and stoned her according to the Sunnah. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and Al-Sha’bi used to mention He witnessed the stoning of Sharahah, and he says that he does not hear anything other than that from the Commander of the Faithful.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8086 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8087","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmed bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Ismail bin Abi Khaled, he said: I heard Al-Sha’bi and he was asked: Did you see the Commander of the Faithful Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him? He said: I saw him. He has a white head and beard. It was said: Do you remember anything about him? He said: Yes, I remember that he flogged Sharaha on Thursday and stoned her on Friday. He said: “I flogged her according to the Book of God and stoned her according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” This is an authentic chain of narration, although in the first chain of transmission there is a disagreement regarding the hearing of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud from his father
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8087 - True"
"8088","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Tell me Muhammad bin Talha bin Yazid bin Rukana, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought Upon him, he greeted a Jew and a Jewish woman who had committed adultery while they had been married to each other. So they asked him to judge them, so he judged them by stoning, so he stoned them both before The mosque in Bani Ghanam. When he found that he was touching the stones, he went to his friend and bent over her to protect her from touching the stones, and it was what God had made. of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he stood up to her to protect her from the stones. Other than the people of the profession are under the illusion that this Ismail Al-Shaybani is unknown, but this is not the case, as Amr bin Dinar Al-Athram narrated from him.”"
"8089","As Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ismail Al-Shaybani, who said: I sold what was in the heads of my palm trees for one hundred wasqs. If there is more, then it is theirs, and if there is less, then it is theirs. So I asked Ibn Umar. May God be pleased with them, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade that, but he permitted the matter of being naked.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8089 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8090","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of my father Bishr, on the authority of Khaled bin Arfata, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in A man had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl and said: “If she is permissible for him, he will be flogged with one hundred lashes, and if she is not permissible for him, then she will stone him.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8090 - True"
"8091","Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrafi informed us of the passing of Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl. Hafs bin Omar Al-Adni told us, Al-Hakam bin told us. He stated, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever among the Muslims opposes his religion So kill him, and when the servant says, “I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger,” then there is no way for us to him except by his right. “It is correct that it should be established as it is.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8091 - Al-Adani is perished"
"8092","Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaim Al-Shaybani informed us, in Kufa, Ahmed bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath, told us My father, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “There was a man from the Ansar who converted to Islam and then apostatized and joined polytheism.” Then he regretted it and sent to his people to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, whether I can repent? He said: Then “How will God guide a people who disbelieved after they had believed and bore witness that the Messenger is true and to them clear proofs had come” was revealed [Al Imran: 86] - to his saying - {Except those who repent after that and make amends. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving, Merciful} [Al Imran: 89] He said: “Then his people came to him and he submitted.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8092 - True"
"8093","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Imam and Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb informed us, then Abu Hammam Muhammad bin Muhabab, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Haritha bin Mudarib, on the authority of Al-Furat bin Hayyan, and he was an Ain Abu Sufyan and an ally, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had ordered his killing, so he passed by a group of the Ansar and said: I am a Muslim, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, among you are men whom We call to their faith, among them is Al-Furat ibn Hayyan.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and it was not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8093 - True"
"8094","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Ali bin Salih told us, about Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, who said: “There were Qurayzah and An-Nadir, and he was one of the nobles of Qurayzah, so he was If a man from the Qurayzah kills a man from the Nadir, he will be killed by him, and if a man from the Nadir kills a man from the Qurayzah, they say: Give him to us and we will kill him. They said: Between us and you is the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they brought him, and it was revealed: {And if you judge, judge between them with justice. Indeed, God loves those who are just.} [Al-Ma’idah: 42] A life for a life, then “Are the wise men of pre-Islamic times seeking to seek”? [Al-Ma’idah: 50] “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8094 - True"
"8095","Abu Amr told us Othman bin Ahmed bin Abdullah Al-Daqqaq, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Malaab bin Hayyan told us, Abu Amir told us Al-Aqdi, Ibrahim bin Tahman told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in three cases: a married adulterer and he will be stoned, and a man who kills intentionally and he will be killed.” And he will be crucified, or he will be exiled from the earth. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8095 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8096","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Hisham bin Ali Al-Sadusi told us, Yahya bin Abdullah told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only blinded the eyes of the shepherds because they blinded the eyes of the shepherds.”"
"8097","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told us, Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Al-Nadr Al-Jaruudi told us, Al-Fadl bin Sahl Al-Araj, Yahya bin Abdullah told us, and he mentioned with a similar chain of transmission: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8096 - That in Muslim"
"8098","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever kills his servant, We will kill him.” And whoever berates his servant, We will reward him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it. “And there is evidence for it from the hadith of Abu Hurairah.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8098 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"8099","Abd al-Baqi bin Qani’ al-Hafiz told us in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Yahya bin al-Mundhir, and Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb told us: Othman bin Al-Haytham, the muezzin of the Basra Mosque, told us. Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills his servant, We will kill him, and whoever kills his servant, We will kill him.” Al-Hakim said: “I fear that Othman bin Al-Haytham wanted the first chain of transmission as narrated by Yazid bin Harun, and God knows best."
"8100","So Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Bundar told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, he told me My father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever castrates his servant, We will castrate him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8100 - True"
"8101","Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad, the jurist, and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Ismail al-Qaari informed us, saying: Uthman ibn Sa`id al-Darimi told us, Abdullah bin Saleh told us, Al-Layth bin Saad told me, on the authority of Omar bin Isa Al-Qurashi, then Al-Asadi, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: A slave girl came to Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and she said: My master accused me. So he made me sit on the fire until my private part was burned. Then Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: Did he see that on you? She said: No, he said: So you confessed something to him? She said: No, Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: Ali, so when Omar, may God be pleased with him, saw the man, he said: Will I be tortured with the punishment of God? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, she accused her about herself. He said: Did you see that about her? The man said: No. He said: So she confessed that to you? He said: No. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, had I not heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A slave shall not be led by its owner, nor a child by His father, “I would have taken it away from you.” So he took him out and struck him with a hundred lashes, then said: Go, for you are free for the sake of God and you are God’s servant. And his Messenger, Abu Salih said: Al-Layth said: “This is to be done.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and he did not narrate it and have two witnesses.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8101 - True"
"8102","Abu Ja`far bin Duhaym told us, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Malik bin Ismail told us, Abu Shihab Abd Rabbuh told us. Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Hamza al-Jazari, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He imitated his servant, for he is free and he is the master of God and His Messenger.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8102 - Hamza is Al-Nasibi who narrates the hadith"
"8103","Abu Ja`far bin Duhaym told us, Ahmad bin Hazim told us, Asim bin Yusuf al-Yarbu’i told us, Abtar bin Qasim told us, Husayn told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf said: We were staying at the house of Suwayd bin Muqrin, and with us was an ignorant old man, so I do not know what the daughter of Suwayd said, so he slapped her and became angry. From that, he became so angry that he had never been so angry. He said: “You are unable to do anything except the heat of her face. You saw me as the seventh of seven of the Banu Muqrin. We have nothing but “One servant, the youngest of us, slapped her, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered us to free her.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8103 - True"
"8104","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ubaid bin Sharik told us, Abu Al-Jamahir Muhammad bin Uthman told us, Saeed bin Bashir told us, Saeed bin Bashir told us Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A son is not led by his father. Punishment punishments shall not be imposed in mosques.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8104 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8105","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal, Muhammad bin Ayyub, and Abu Ja`far al-Hadrami told us, they said: Abu Kurayb reported, on the authority of Abdullah bin Idris, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he smote and hid, and that Abu Bakr smote and hid, and Omar, he smote and hid. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8105 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8106","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi told me, Muawiyah ibn Amr told us, Muawiyah ibn Amr told us Zaida, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Ali, may God be pleased with him, made a speech and said: O People, establish the punishments on your female slaves, those of them who are chaste and those who are not, for a female slave of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, committed adultery, so the Messenger of God commanded me God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me to flog her, so I went to her, and behold, she had recently died of bleeding. I was afraid that if I flogged her, I would kill her or She died, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, and he said: “You have done well.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8106 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8107","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Bukayr Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Ashjaj narrated to him. He said - While I was sitting with Suleiman Ibn Yasar when Abd al-Rahman Ibn Jabir entered - he narrated to Suleiman. Ibn Yassar, and he said: Abd al-Rahman Ibn Jabir told me that his father told him that he heard Abu Burdah al-Ansari, may God be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “He shall not be flogged with more than ten lashes except within the limits set by God Almighty.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8107 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8108","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Musa Al-Tamimi told us, Manjab bin Al-Harith told us, Abd Al-Malik told us Ibn Harun Ibn Antarah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Amr Ibn Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, that he visited his paternal aunt and she prayed for him with food. Then the maid slowed down and said: Aren’t you in a hurry, you adulteress? Then Amr said: Glory be to God, you have said a great matter. Have you informed about her matter? Adultery? She said: No, by God. Amr, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whichever slave or woman said Or she said to her daughter, “You adulteress,” and she did not find out about her adultery. She will flog her and her daughter on the Day of Resurrection, because there will be no limit to them in This world” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. “But they agreed in this matter on the hadith of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, said: “Whoever slanders his slaves with adultery, the punishment will be imposed on him on the Day of Resurrection.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8108 - Rather, Abd al-Malik ibn Harun was abandoned by consensus until he was called an antichrist."
"8109","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Muslim bin Khalid told us, Abu Hazim told us, he told me Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “A man from Islam came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: “He committed adultery with a woman who he named her and she denied it, so he separated him and left her.” This is an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it, and he witnessed it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8109 - True"
"8110","What Muhammad bin Salih bin Hani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musa bin Harun Al-Bardi told us, Hisham bin Yusuf, Al-Qasim bin Fayyad Al-Anbari told us, on the authority of Khallad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. A man from Banu Bakr bin Laith came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and confessed that he had committed adultery with a woman four times, so he was flogged one hundred times, and he was a virgin. Then he asked him for evidence on the woman, and the woman said: He lied, by God, O Messenger of God, so he was flogged to the extent of libel for eighty years. “This is an authentic hadith.” The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8110 - Al-Qasim bin Fayyad is weak"
"8111","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan Al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Saeed bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, about Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that Hilal bin Umayyah slandered his wife in the presence of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Sharik bin Excuse me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Evidence or punishment in your back.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8111 - True"
"8112","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Al-Qanabi told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of his uncle Al-Harith bin Abd. The Most Gracious, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said regarding wine: “If he drinks it, flog him. “He returns, flog him, but if he returns on the fourth day, then kill him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. “And on the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, Abdullah bin Omar, and Shuhrabil bin Aws - and these are among the Companions, may God be pleased with them.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8112 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8113","So Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Dawud bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Khaled bin Hazm, on the authority of Jarir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he drinks wine Then flog him, and if he returns, flog him. If he returns, then flog him. If he returns on the fourth day, then kill him.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8113 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8114","So Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim told us, Ubayy told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Abi Na’am, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol, flog him, and if he drinks “Then flog him. If he drinks, flog him. If he drinks, kill him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8114 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8115","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl, told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abu Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol, flog him, then He drinks, flog him, then when he drinks, flog him, then when he drinks on the fourth day, kill him.” This chain of transmission is authentic according to Muslim’s condition, and he did not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8115 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8116","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari told us, Abu Abdullah Al-Bushangi told us, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abd Al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, On the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol So flog him, then when he drinks, flog him, then when he drinks, flog him, then when he drinks on the fourth day, kill him.” Mu’ammar said: So I narrated to him. Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir said: “That has been abandoned after that. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brought Ibn Al-Nu’ayman and flogged him, then he was brought to him and he flogged him, then he was brought He flogged him, then he was brought on the fourth day and he was flogged and nothing more than that.” As for the hadith of Muawiyah:"
"8117","So Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abd Al-Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed told us on the authority of Asim bin Bahdala, on the authority of Abu Salih, who praised him well, on the authority of Muawiyah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If they drink If they drink wine, flog them. Then if they drink, flog them. Then if they drink, flog them. Then if they drink the fourth, kill them.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8117 - True"
"8118","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If one of you drinks alcohol, flog him, and then if he returns So flog him, and if he returns on the fourth day, then kill him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8118 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8119","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Muadh bin Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said regarding wine: “If they drink it, flog them. Then if they drink it, flog them. Then if they drink it, flog them. Then if they drink it, flog them. They drink it, so kill them at the fourth hour.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8119 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8120","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Khalaf bin Salem, and Abdullah bin Amr Al-Iraqi told us, They said: Muhammad bin Ja’far Ghandar told us, Shu’bah told us on the authority of Abu Bishr, he said: I heard Yazid bin Abi Kabsha, delivering a sermon in the Levant. He said: I heard a man from the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, speaking to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan about wine, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in Concerning alcohol: “If he drinks it, flog him. If he drinks it again, flog him. Then if he drinks it again, flog him. Then if he returns on the fourth day, then kill him.” I heard Abu Ali Al-Hafiz, narrating this hadith to us, said at the end of it: This companion from the people of the Levant is Sharhabeel bin Aws."
"8121","So he narrated to us the authenticity of what Abu Ali Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani mentioned, narrated to us Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Burd Al-Antaki narrated to us, narrated to us Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ al-Bahrani, Jarir bin Othman told us, on the authority of Abi Al-Hasan Nimran bin Muhammad, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Aws, and he was one of the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If he drinks alcohol, flog him, then if he drinks, flog him, then if he drinks So flog him, then if he drinks the fourth time, kill him.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8121 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8122","As for the hadith of Al-Nadr, from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever drinks alcohol, flog him. If he returns, flog him. If he returns, flog him. If he returns the fourth time, then kill him.”"
"8123","Ziyad bin Abdullah told us, Ibn Ishaq told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar, and he said: “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck Al-Nu’ayman four times.”"
"8124","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us about it, Abu Qalaba told us about it, Abu Asim told us about it, Ibn Jurayj told us about it, Muhammad bin told me about it. Ali bin Rukana, Ikrimah told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not put time in the wine.” Haddad” Ibn Abbas said: A man drank and became drunk at dawn, so we took him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he approached Abbas’s house, he escaped. So he entered upon Al-Abbas, and he committed himself to him. He mentioned that to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he laughed and said: “Did he do it?” He did not command anything about it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8124 - True"
"8125","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuhli told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul Wahhab told us, Ayoub narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith, who said: “Then Nu’ayman or Ibn Nu’ayman was brought as a drinker, so the Messenger ordered God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded whoever was in the house to hit him. He said: “And I was among those who hit him, so we hit him with sandals and a leaf.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “Abd al-Warith ibn Sa`id and Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi continued to connect it with the mention of Uqba ibn Al-Harith
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8125 - True"
"8126","Abu Sa`id Ahmad ibn Ya`qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf ibn Ya`qub al-Qadi told us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr told us, Abd al-Warith told us, Ayoub told us, On the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: Uqba bin Al-Harith told me, he said: “Al-Nu’ayman was brought and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered those in the house to They struck him with their hands and sandals, and I was among those who struck him.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8126 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8127","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan Al-Sayrifi told us about Marw, Abd Al-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Ju'ayd bin Abdul-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifa, on the authority of Al-Sa'ib bin Yazid, who said: “The drinker was brought during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and in the command of Abu Bakr and a leader of the command of Omar, may God be pleased with them both, we rise up to him and strike him with our hands and sandals. And you brought us back, until he came from the emirate of Umar, and he was flogged forty therein, until when they rebelled there and were immoral, he was flogged therein eighty.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8127 - This in Al-Bukhari"
"8128","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us about... Abu Salamah, and Yahya bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Azhar, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought. He greeted him with a mustache and said: “Go to him and beat him.” So they stood up to him and stamped him with their sandals. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8128 - True"
"8129","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Abu Al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: I will not drink draft wine after it was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with something drunk. He said: O Messenger of God, I did not drink wine, but I drank raisin wine and dates in a bowl. “So he ordered that he be shaken with his hands and taped with his sandals. “And he forbade raisins, dates, and creatures.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8129 - True"
"8130","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakkar bin Qutaybah Al-Qadi told us, Safwan bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Usama bin Zaid told us, about Al-Zuhri, said: Abd al-Rahman bin Azhar, may God be pleased with him, told me: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Hunayn, and he was He wandered among the people, asking about the house of Khalid ibn al-Walid. A drunk man was brought, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered whoever was with him to They hit him with whatever was in their hands.” He said: “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, threw dust in his face.” He said: “Then Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, came.” On the authority of him, he was drunk. He said: “So he took aim at those whom he had struck that day, and struck forty.” And he struck ‘Umar, may God be pleased with him, forty."
"8131","Al-Zuhri said: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Buraat Al-Kalbi, he said: Khalid bin Al-Walid sent me to Omar, may God be pleased with them both. So I came to him while he was in the mosque, with him were Othman bin Affan, Ali, Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, Talha, and al-Zubayr, may God be pleased with them, reclining. With him in the mosque, I said: “Khalid bin Al-Walid sent me to you while he was reciting his greetings to you and saying: The people have become absorbed in wine.” They avoided the punishment, so Omar said: These are with you, so ask them. Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: We see him when he is drunk, he becomes delirious, and when he is delirious He slandered, and the slanderer received eighty lashes, so Omar said: Tell your friend what he said: Khalid was given eighty lashes, and Omar was given eighty lashes, and it was Omar when he came. A strong man who has indulged in drinking will be given eighty lashes, and if a weak man who has committed a mistake is brought, he will be given forty lashes, then Othman will be given eighty lashes. Forty: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8131 - True"
"8132","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Baghdadi informed us, Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih told us, Sa`id ibn Kathir ibn Ufeir, Yahya bin Falih Abu Al-Mughirah Al-Khuza’i told us, Thawr bin Zaid Al-Dili told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: Drinkers were beaten during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with their hands, sandals, and a stick, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. May God bless him and grant him peace. They were more numerous during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, than they were during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu said Bakr, may God be pleased with him: If We had imposed a punishment for them and they had chosen something similar to what they were subjected to during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then it would have been Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, flogged them for forty until he died, then Omar rose up after him and also flogged them forty, until a man was brought from The first immigrants, and he had been drinking, so he was ordered to be flogged, and he said: Why do you flog me? There is between you and me the Book of God Almighty, so Omar, may God be pleased with him, said On his authority: In which book of God do you find that I do not flog you? He said: Indeed, God Almighty says in His Book: “There is no blame on those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have tasted” [Al-Ma’idah: 93] Verse, then I am of those who believe. And they did righteous deeds, then they feared and believed, then they feared and did good. I witnessed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Badr, Al-Hudaybiyyah, and Khandaq. And the scenes. Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: Don’t you respond to what he says? Ibn Abbas said: These verses were sent down as an excuse for the past and a proof for those who remain, because God Almighty says: {O you who have believed! Indeed, wine, gambling, stones, and arrows are only an abomination from the work of Satan.} [Al-Ma’idah: 90] Then he recited until he completed the other verse {not according to Those who believe and do righteous deeds will be rewarded with regard to what they ate, since they feared and believed and did righteous deeds, then feared and believed, then feared and did good.} [Al-Maidah: 93] For God Almighty has forbidden drinking alcohol, so Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: You are right, so what do you see? Then Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “We see that when he drinks he becomes drunk, and when he is drunk he becomes delusional, and when he ravens he slanders, and the one who slanders shall bear eighty lashes.” So Omar, may God be pleased with him, ordered He was flogged by eighty people. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8132 - True"
"8133","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, that a woman was a prostitute in pre-Islamic times, and a man passed by her, and he extended his hand to her and touched her. She said: “Mah, God Almighty abolished polytheism and brought Islam, so he left her and turned away and began to look at her until his face became sad.” The wall, he said: Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned that to him, and he said: “You are a servant. God wants good for you. Indeed, when God intends good for a servant “He will hasten the punishment for his sin for him, and if he intends evil, He will withhold the punishment for his sin until he brings it back on the Day of Resurrection as if it were a camel.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8133 - True"
"8134","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Al-Aswad bin Amir Shazan told us, Huraym bin Sufyan told us. Al-Bajli, on the authority of Bayan ibn Bishr, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abu Shahm, who said: I was in Medina and a maid passed by me and took me. Then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was pledging allegiance to the people, and he said to me: “Are you not the owner of the cake yesterday?” I said: I will not come back, O Messenger of God, so he pledged allegiance to me. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, on the condition of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8134 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8135","Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us, in Kufa, Muhammad bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Asbat bin Muhammad Al-Qurashi told us, Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, who said: A man came to Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and said: Do you have anything to do with Al-Walid bin Uqba? Is his beard dripping with wine? He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from spying if it appeared to us so that we could take it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8135 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8136","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-Sana’ani told me about Mecca, which God Almighty has guarded. Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Dabari told us, Abd informed us Al-Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Zurara bin Musab bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, that he guarded the city one night with Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and while they were walking, a lamp lit up for them. In a house, so they set off to visit it until, when they approached it, they saw a door open to people who had loud voices in it. Omar, may God be pleased with him, said: He took Abdul Rahman's hand: Do you know whose house this is? He said: No, he said: This is the house of Rabi’ah bin Umayyah bin Khalaf and they are now drinking, so what do you see? Then Abdul-Rahman said: “I see that we have done what God has forbidden. God Almighty forbade us and said: {And do not spy} [Al-Hujurat: 12]. We have spied “Then Omar turned away from them and left them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8136 - True"
"8137","Abu Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Firas, the Maliki jurist in Mecca, may God Almighty protect it, told us. Abu Bakr bin Sahl al-Damiati told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz Al-Ramli told us, Ismail bin Ayyash told us, Damdam bin Zur’ah told us, on the authority of Shurayh bin Ubaid, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, Kathir bin Murrah, Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, and Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, may God be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The If the prince seeks to create doubt among the people, he corrupts them.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8137 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8138","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told me, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Imam told me, Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Zuhayr bin Hunaid told me, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Abdullah Al-Basri, on the authority of Zufar Ibn Thaymah, on the authority of Hakim Ibn Hazzam, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not recite poems in the mosques, and do not carry out punishments therein.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8138 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"8139","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abu Kurayb told us, Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, Hisham told us Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not make a cut for less than one-eighth.” A shield, a shield, or a shield, and both of them will be worth a price on that day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8139 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8140","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “God has cursed the thief who steals an egg, his hand will be cut off, and if he steals “His hand was cut off.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8140 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8141",""
"8142","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zur’ah Al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Musa, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “It was the price of a shield during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It is worth ten dirhams.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but he did not narrate it, and the hadith of Ayman bears witness to it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8142 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8143","Ali bin Hamshadh, Al-Adl told us, Yazid bin Al-Haytham told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Al-Layth told us, Al-Ashja’i told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ayman, he said: “The hand was not amputated during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for the price of a shield.” Its price on that day will be a dinar.” I heard Abu Abbas, saying: I heard Al-Rabi’, saying: I heard Al-Shafi’i, saying: “This Ayman is the son of a woman.” Ka'b and not the son of Umm Ayman, and he did not reach the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"8144",""
"8145","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told me, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told me, Suleiman bin Daoud Al-Hashimi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi told us. Al-Zinad, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: A woman was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who had stolen So she sought refuge with the stepson of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it had been Fatima, I would have cut off her hand.” So he cut off her hand."
"8146","Then Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Isfaraini informed us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Al-Baraa told us, Ali bin Al-Madini told us, he said: “He was the stepson of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Salama bin Abi Salamah only sought refuge with the Makhzoumiya woman who had stolen with one of them. The two sheikhs agreed to narrate the hadith. Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Makhzoumiya only sought refuge with Usama bin Zaid, and this is correct.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8145 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8147","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Zur’ah Al-Dimashqi told us, Ahmad bin Khaled Al-Wahbi told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha bin Shaddad bin Rukana, on the authority of his mother Aisha bint Masoud bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of her father Masoud, he said: When she stole That beautiful woman from the house of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We honored that, and she was a woman from Quraysh. So we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we spoke to him and said: O Messenger of God, we will pay the ransom for her with forty uqiyah. He said: “Purification is better for her.” When we heard his statement The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, we came to Usama bin Zaid and said: Intercede on our behalf with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding this woman. We ransomed it with forty uqiyah. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw the seriousness of the people in this matter, he stood up and preached, and said: “O people, what is the matter? Your exaggeration in one of God’s punishments fell upon a female slave of God, and by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, had come down with that With this woman, Muhammad cut off her hand. He said: Then the people despaired, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cut off her hand. Muhammad bin Ishaq said: Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told me, “After that, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had mercy on her and prayed for her.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not produce it in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8147 - True"
"8148","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, and Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, They said: Abu Asim Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid Al-Shaybani told us, Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Safwan bin Umayyah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man who had stolen a suit of his, then he said: O Messenger of God, give it to me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “So, before you bring it to us.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and the hadith explained in it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8148 - True"
"8149","What Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Talha Al-Qannad told us, Asbat bin Nasr Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Humaid Ibn Safwan’s sister, on the authority of Safwan bin Umayyah, he said: I was sleeping in The mosque, and I had a khamisah worth thirty dirhams, and a man came and stole it from me. The man was taken and brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered He wanted it to be cut, so I came to him and said: Will you cut it for thirty dirhams? I will sell it and forget its price. He said: “Can this be done before you bring it to me?”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8149 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8150","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Ibrahim bin Hamza told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Yazid bin Khusaifa told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace A thief was brought to him who had stolen a sheep, and they said: O Messenger of God, this man has stolen. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I don’t think he has stolen.” The thief said: Yes, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go with him and cut him, then cut him, then bring him to me.” So he was cut and then He was brought, and he said: “Repent to God.” He said: “Repent to God,” and he said: “May God repent to you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8150 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8151","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man from Muzainah came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, how do you see Harissa in the mountain? He said: “It is like it, and the punishment does not involve cutting any of the livestock, except for what it took on board and reached the cage, then there are pieces in it, and whatever it did not reach.” “For the price of a shield, there is a double fine and floggings.”
 He said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of the hanging fruit? He said: “It is the same and something like it with it, and there is no cut in any of the hanging fruit, except what the green tree sheltered and reached the price of a spear, in which there are pieces, and unless It is equivalent to the price of a demon, so there is a fine equal to it and severe lashes.” This is a Sunnah that was unique to Amr bin Shuaib bin Muhammad, on the authority of his grandfather Abd “If the narrator, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, is trustworthy, then he is like Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar.”"
"8152","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Khuza’i told us that Mecca was protected by God Almighty. Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Zakaria bin Abi told us Masara, Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, Saeed bin Abi Ayyub told us, Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Nayyar, may God be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “He shall not be flogged with more than ten lashes within the limits set by God Almighty.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission is based on the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8152 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8153","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hasan bin Al-Harbi told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Hammad bin Al-Harbi told us. Salama, Yusuf bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Hatib, that a man stole during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Kill him.” They said: He only stole. He said: “Cut him down.” Then he stole again and was cut off, then he stole during the reign of Abu Bakr and was cut off, then he stole and was cut off until his legs were cut off, then he stole the fifth, and Abu said Bakr, may God be pleased with him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, knew about this when he ordered his killing. Go and kill him, so he was sent to Young men from Quraysh, among whom was Abdullah bin Al-Zubair. Abdullah bin Al-Zubair said: Command me over you. So they appointed him, and when he struck him, they beat him until They killed him. “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8153 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"8154","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Abu Muhammad Fahd bin Sulayman told us in Egypt, Musa bin Daoud al-Dhabi told us, Sufyan told us Bin Saeed Al-Thawri, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If the remaining slave steals, he is not obligated to take a piece, nor is the non-Muslim obligated.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. Its chain of narration was the only one Musa bin Dawud, who is one of the trustworthy men, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8154 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8155","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Wahb bin Jarir told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, and Ahmad bin Ja'far al-Quta'i, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja'far told us, on the authority of Shu'bah, he said: I heard Yahya Al-Jaber, saying: I heard Abu Majida, saying: I was sitting with Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, and he said: I do not remember the first A man was cut off by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. A thief was brought and he ordered him to be cut off, as if he had grieved the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Messenger of God, it is as if you disliked cutting him off. He said: “And what prevents me? Do not be helpers of Satan against your brother. It is not appropriate for the imam to God is Forgiving and loves to pardon. And let them pardon and forgive. Don’t you like for God to forgive you? And God is Forgiving. “Merciful.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8155 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8156","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, he said: I heard Ibn Jurayj, speaking on the authority of Amr Ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Establish the boundaries between yourselves, for whatever punishment that has reached me is obligatory.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8156 - True"
"8157","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Ahmad bin Bishr al-Murtadi narrated to us, Bishr bin Muadh narrated to us, Abdullah bin Jaafar narrated to us, narrated to me Muslim bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamer bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said And he said: “Whoever’s intercession is prevented beyond the limits of God’s limits, then he has opposed God Almighty in his matter.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8157 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8158","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, Asad bin Musa told us, Anas bin Iyad told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, Abdullah bin Dinar told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said after he was stoned Al-Islami, and he said: “Avoid this filth that God has forbidden. Whoever suffers, let him cover himself with God’s cover and repent to God.” “For whoever reveals his identity to us, we will punish him with the Book of God Almighty.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8158 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8159","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hisham bin Hassan informed us, On the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever covers his brother in This world will be covered by God in this world and the hereafter, and whoever relieves his brother of the distress of this world, God will relieve him of the distress of the Day of Resurrection, and God will help the servant as long as the servant is helping his brother.” This chain of transmission is correct according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8159 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8160","Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad al-Anbari told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Salam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Hayyan bin Hilal, Wahib told us, Suhail told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “No servant should cover himself.” A slave in this world, except that God will cover him on the Day of Resurrection.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And this authenticates the hadith of Al-A’mash. On the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A servant does not conceal another servant in this world except that he conceals it.” Allah on the Day of Resurrection.” And that is because Asbat bin Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated it on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Abu Salih, and Hammad narrated it Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Wasi’, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Salih
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8160 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8161","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammam bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, said: Shaybah Al-Khudari narrated to me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “There are three things I swear upon, and on the fourth, if I had sworn upon him, I would hope that I would not be a sinner. God does not make a servant who has a share in Islam like one who He has no share, and no servant of God takes over in this world and someone else will take him over on the Day of Resurrection, and no man loves a people unless he is with them or among them, And the fourth: If I had sworn on her, I would have hoped that I would not be a sinner. God does not cover a servant in this world except that God will cover him in the Hereafter. He said: So I narrated. Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and Omar said: “If you heard such a hadith on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And peace be upon him, so guard him and guard him.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8161 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8162","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibrahim bin Nashit, on the authority of Ka’b, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Kathir, the client of Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who “He saw a private matter and covered it. It was as if he had made a woman shy from her grave.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8162 - True"
"8163","Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari informed us, Abu Al-Mujih informed us, Abdan informed us, Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Ziyad. Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Avert the borders from Muslims as much as you are able. If you find a way out for a Muslim, then let him go. For the Imam to make a mistake in forgiving is better than to make a mistake. “With punishment.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
 Khallad bin Yahya, Bashir bin Al-Muhajir told us, Ibn Buraidah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: “We, as companions of Muhammad, would talk if a goat or This woman did not come at four o’clock. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not ask for her. “Sahih”"
"8164","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told me, he told me Asim bin Amr bin Qatada, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Qatada bin Al-Numan, may God be pleased with him, said: Banu Ubayraq were a group of Banu Zafar, and there were three of them: Bashir, Bashir, and Mubashir, and Bashir was nicknamed Abu Tu’ma. He was a poet, and he was a hypocrite, and he used to say poetry to satire. The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he says: So-and-so said it. When that reaches them, they say: The enemy of God has lied. He only said it. He, he said:
[full sea]

Whenever the men recited a poem... they urged me to tell Abiraq that he said it.
Snorting as if I feared them... God cut their noses and made them clear.
They were poor and needy people during pre-Islamic times and Islam, and my uncle Rifa’ah bin Zayd was a well-to-do man who converted to Islam. By God, if I would have thought that there was something in his conversion to Islam, and whenever he had a left hand, this cloud of mist would come upon him, carrying the drums he had bought. For himself what befalls him,As for his children, he was protecting them with barley, so a maid - they were the Nabataeans - came carrying a drum, so Rifa’a bought two loads of barley and put them in An attic of his own, and in his attic were two of his shields and some of their tools that could fit them, so a good tidings knocked on him during the night and broke through the attic from its back. So he took the food, then he took the weapon. When morning came, my uncle sent for me, so I came to him and said: We were attacked this night, and he took our food. And our weapons. Bashir and his brothers said: By God, there is no one in charge of your goods except Labid bin Sahl - a man from among us who was noble and upright - so when he reached him, He said: By God, I prayed with the sword. Then he said: That is, Bani Al-Abiraq, and I am stealing. By God, this sword will come into contact with you, or you will make clear who The one who committed this theft. They said: Leave us, for by God, you are innocent of this theft. He said: No, and you have claimed. Then we asked us at home. We spied until we were told: By God, the Banu Ubayraq have been awake tonight and we only see them on your food. So we continued until we were almost certain. They are his companions, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I spoke to him about them, and I said: O Messenger of God, the people of a household among us are people of cruelty. They attacked my uncle with foolishness, so they tore down his upper room and took food and weapons.As for food, we have no need for it. As for weapons, let him return it to us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I will look into that,” and they had A cousin called Asir bin Urwa, so he gathered the men of his people and then came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Rifa’ah bin Zaid and Ibn His brother, Qatada bin Al-Numan, deliberately attacked a household among us who were people of lineage, honor, and righteousness. They denounced them with evil and denounced them with theft. Without evidence or testimony, he put it with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said whatever he wanted with his tongue, then he left, and I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted me and I spoke to him, and he made a strong face at me and said: “Wretched is what you have done and wretched is what you have walked through. And it is valid to accuse them of theft and blame them for it without proof or proof.” So I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something I disliked. So I left him and wished I had gone out of my money and not spoken to him. When I returned home, my uncle sent to me: O son of my brother, what have you done? So I said: By God, I wish I had gone out of my money and not spoken to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it. By God, I would never return to him. So he said: By God The helper,Then the Qur’an was revealed: “Indeed, We have sent down to you the Book with the truth that you may judge between the people according to what God has shown you, and do not be an adversary to the traitors.” [An-Nisa: 105] meaning, To’mah. Ibn Abiraq, so he recited until he reached the age of lest they mislead you} [An-Nisa: 113] meaning Asir bin Urwah and his companions, then he said: {There is no good in much of their secret conversations} [An-Nisa: 114] - to His saying - {And He forgives anything other than that to whom He wills} [An-Nisa: 48] whatever his sin was, short of polytheism. When the Qur’an was revealed, he fled and joined Mecca and was sent The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, handed over to me the two shields and their tools, and he placed them in a state of honor. Qatada said: When I brought them and what was with them, he said: O son of my brother, they are in the cause of God Almighty, so I hoped that my uncle had converted to Islam well. My suspicion of him was other than that, and Ibn Abiraq went out until he came to Salama bint Saad bin Sahl, the sister of Banu Amr bin Awf, and she was With Talha bin Abi Talha in Mecca, he found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions insulting them, so Hassan bin Thabit shot him. In verses, he said:
[Long Sea]

O thief of the two shields, if you remember... I bid farewell to him who was generous among men.
Bint Saad revealed it in the morning...He fights with her to flog his lover and she fights with him
So, as a prisoner, you came to your neighbor desiring... him, and you did not intend to defend him?
You thought that what you had done would be hidden...and among you is a prophet who has the revelation and who set it.
Were it not for men among you whom you insult... for that, calamities have befallen him.
So if you mention Ka'b according to what you have attributed... Is there any human being that does not have legs?
I found them hoping for you, you have already known... just as rain is hoped for by a fat person and follows it.
When she reached Hassan’s hair, she took Ubareq’s sack and placed it on her head until she threw it with a pellet, then she shaved, scalded, and pierced it. And if you had spent a dark night in my house and had given me the poetry of Hassan ibn Thabit, you would not have shown me any good. When I took him out, he followed Taif. So he entered a house where there was no one, and it fell on him and killed him. The Quraysh began to say: By God, no good will leave Muhammad among his companions. This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8164 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8165","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told me about irrigation, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Yunus bin Abi told us Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever commits a sin in This world, so God will protect him and pardon him. God is too generous to go back on something. He has pardoned him and covered him, and whoever commits a sin in this world. So he was punished for it. God is more just than punishing a servant twice. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. Evidence of the increase in words and recitation of the Qur’an in it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8165 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8166","Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Baghawi told us, Jeddi told us, Thawr bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Marwan bin Muawiyah, On the authority of Azhar bin Rashid Al-Kahili, on the authority of Abu Sukhaila, he said: The Commander of the Faithful Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said to us: Shall I not inform you? With the best verse in the Book of God Almighty, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: {Whatever calamity befalls you} [Al-Shura: 30] of what you have earned. your hands and pardons many. “For God is too generous to spare them punishment, and whatever God pardons in this world, God is too generous to return to them.” In his pardon
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8166 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8167","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Usama bin Zaid told me that Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, narrated to him that Ibn Khuzaymah bin Thabit narrated to him, on the authority of his father, Khuzaymah bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Any servant who commits something of what God has forbidden and then the punishment is imposed on him, that sin will be expiated from him.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8167 - True"
"8168","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani informed us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab informed us, Ja`far bin Aoun informed us, he informed us Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, was brought with an affliction that had broken out, so he ordered He stoned her, so Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, passed by her and the boys were following her, and he said: “What is this?” They said: Omar ordered her to be stoned. He said: He sent her back and went with her to Omar, may God be pleased with him, and said: “Did you not know that the pen was lifted from An insane person until he regains his senses, and an afflicted person until he regains his senses, and a sleeper until he wakes up, and a child until he has a wet dream.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions The two sheikhs did not narrate it. “And Shu’bah narrated it, on the authority of Al-A’mash, with additional wording.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8168 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8169","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl and Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi narrated to us, saying: Al-Harith bin Abi Usama narrated to us, Abu Al-Nadr narrated to us, Shu'bah, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, was brought to a woman. An insane woman was pregnant, so he wanted to stone her, so Ali said to him: “Did you not know that the pen has been lifted from three things: from the insane person until he regains his senses; And on behalf of a boy until he has a wet dream, and on behalf of a sleeper until he wakes up, “and he left her.” This hadith was narrated with an authentic chain of transmission on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a chain of transmission.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8169 - It is authentic that there is a transmission"
"8170","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, I am Ali bin Abdul Aziz, Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The pen has been lifted from three people: from the sleeper until he wakes up, from the insane person until he becomes sensible, and from the child until he awakens.” jasper"
"8171","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Hashim bin Marthad al-Tabarani told us, Amr bin al-Rabi’ bin Tariq told us, Ikrimah told us Bin Ibrahim, Sa`id bin Abi Arouba told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, may God be pleased with him, that He was with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on a journey. He entered and people gathered around him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, the Pen was lifted from three people: from “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8171 - Ikrimah weak"
"8172","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abu Wahb told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Atiya, a man from Banu Qurayzah told him, “The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stripped him on the day of Qurayzah.” They did not see the consolations running over his hair - meaning his pubic hair - so they spared him from being killed.” This is a strange and authentic hadith, and they did not narrate it, but it is known from the hadith Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Atiya al-Qurazi “
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8172 - Sahih Gharib"
"8173","Just as Abu Bakr bin Ishaq narrated to us, Bishr bin Musa narrated to us, Al-Humaidi narrated to us, and Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Muslim narrated to us, Ali bin Al-Madini, all on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Umair, who said: I heard Atiya Al-Qurazi saying: “I was a boy on the day Sa’d ruled Ibn Muadh regarding the Banu Qurayza that their fighter should be killed and their descendants taken captive, but they doubted me and did not find that I made hair grow, so here I am among you.” ""The last book of borders"""
